7. EFM 5.4 Primary Health Check

EFM 5.4 provides a primary health-check mechanism that can be used by a Load Balancer.

Configure the EFM property:

primary.health.check.port=8080

on each PostgreSQL/EFM node.

The Load Balancer performs an HTTP health check against the EFM endpoint.

Expected behavior:

Node 1 :8080 → HTTP 200 → PRIMARY
Node 2 :8080 → HTTP 404 → NOT PRIMARY
Node 3 :8080 → HTTP 404 → NOT PRIMARY
Node 4 :8080 → HTTP 404 → NOT PRIMARY

The Load Balancer should therefore make only the node returning HTTP 200 eligible for PostgreSQL client traffic.

This is preferable to using only a TCP/5432 health check.

A TCP/5432 check only confirms that PostgreSQL is reachable; it does not reliably establish which node is currently the primary.

