Phase 1 – Network Preparation

Confirm:

- Qlik → LB connectivity
- LB → all PostgreSQL nodes
- LB → EFM health-check port
- Firewall rules
- Routing between subnets

Phase 2 – EFM Configuration

Configure:

primary.health.check.port=8080

on all EFM database nodes.

Validate the endpoint behavior.

Phase 3 – Load Balancer Configuration

Create:

- Frontend listener
- Backend pool
- PostgreSQL TCP service
- EFM HTTP health check
- Primary-only backend selection

Phase 4 – DNS

Create:

postgres-ha.company.com

and point it to the Load Balancer frontend.

Phase 5 – Qlik

Configure Qlik with:

Host: postgres-ha.company.com
Port: 5432

No individual PostgreSQL node IP should be required.

Phase 6 – Testing

Execute controlled failover and connection recovery tests.

