23. Architecture Outcome

The proposed solution achieves the required design objective:

                     ONE QLIK ENDPOINT

                           ↓

                  postgres-ha.company.com

                           ↓

                    Enterprise LB

                           ↓

              Current EFM PRIMARY NODE

During an EFM failover, the database role changes without requiring a change to the Qlik configuration.

The solution therefore provides a stable application-facing endpoint while preserving EFM as the authoritative PostgreSQL HA mechanism.

---

24. Recommendation

Proceed with an Enterprise Load Balancer + FQDN + EFM 5.4 primary health-check architecture.

The recommended production pattern is:

Qlik → FQDN → Enterprise Load Balancer → PostgreSQL 16 nodes

with:

EFM 5.4 → primary health status → Load Balancer → primary-only routing

This design meets the single-endpoint requirement, avoids the need for a cross-subnet PostgreSQL VIP, avoids introducing HAProxy/Pgpool-II, and preserves the existing PostgreSQL/EFM HA architecture.